PW PBE0 spin-polarized Fe with uneven k-point pools.

Three k points per spin are distributed over kpar=2 pools (2+1), so one
pool has no local target k point during the last ACE step in each spin
channel. This exercises the active/idle source-q communication fixed by
PR #8070; the previous implementation fails with MPI_ERR_TRUNCATE.

Run with an even number of MPI ranks, at least two; the CPU test suite
uses four. The reference was generated with kpar=1 and four MPI ranks.
The final total/absolute moments are approximately 0.666667/0.699096
mu_B per cell (FM). A 12 Ry cutoff and 3.0 Angstrom cell keep this small
regression test fast; they are not a cutoff/k-point convergence study.
Energy, forces and total/absolute moments are checked by the existing
integration harness. magnetism.ref opts into the moment comparison
with a tolerance of 1e-3 mu_B per cell.
No ELF output or new test driver is required.
